# proto-file: proto/stipulator/v1/records.proto
# proto-message: stipulator.v1.BindingSet
# Scalar test claims retain their finite populations and declared clause scopes.
# TestTransferKernelSubtractBorrowProperties uses boundary pairs and 256 generated
# valuations per 8-, 32- and 64-bit width, including both carry inputs.
# TestTransferKernelShiftLeft32Properties crosses all 256 CL values with six
# boundary words and adds 512 generated valuations, comparing defined flags only.
# TestTransitionScalarShiftGuardedFlags crosses five count domains with four
# metadata states; TestTransitionScalarShiftGuarantees checks six count domains
# with CMP/SBB predecessors, joined count relations and four sampled valuations.
# TestTransitionScalarDescriptorPopulation checks 2,440 scalar spellings with one
# generated state each. TestRawScalarPopulation checks 26,112 raw encoding tuples.
# TestTransitionScalarEvolvingState checks 288 seven-operation sequences at every
# cut; FuzzTransitionScalarSequence caps generated evolving sequences at 16 ops.
# TestTransitionScalarBorrowBoundaryPopulation crosses 16 words and both carries.
# TestTransitionScalarZeroCountPreservesEntryFlags crosses 16 GPRs and three
# masked-zero counts. Shift-consumer and pointer-lane tests retain their finite
# count/branch and low/high-byte cases; none exhausts the full state product.
# TestTransitionScalarAssemblyOracle compares 250 amd64 hardware cases with
# independently calculated values and defined flags, not universal CPU behavior.
# TestTransitionScalarUnavailablePredicateJoin crosses both shifted-arm placements
# with overwrite, carry and unavailable signed consumers, directly and continued.
# TestTransitionScalarPredicateMergeAvailability crosses either missing operand
# with symbolic and literal guards, retaining unrelated predicates and work counts.
# Occurrence claims below are clause-scoped finite checks, not universal proofs.
# TestOccurrenceOracle* qualifies the independent intent interpreter, event
# inventory and encoding; those reference-only tests do not exercise the checker.
# TestTransitionOccurrenceJointPopulation compares production prefix and completed
# return evidence for 18 shapes (three placements, three payloads, two layouts),
# each with four selector classes and two value variants: 144 joint valuations.
# JointSupplements adds 16 executions: eight outcome-selected exits, four repeated
# selector queries and four mixed query/CAS sequences. These are bounded grammars,
# not complete instruction, input-state, path or outcome populations.
# The joint comparator checks current registers, vectors, flags, byte memory,
# represented provenance and pointer lanes, independently written-bit masks,
# exact occurrence IDs, guards, interleaved events and active frames. Optional
# joined provenance may conservatively disappear; required coordinates may not.
# Inactive CPUID controls use two baseline assignments and independently perturb
# each inactive occurrence's response lanes; sensitivity controls expose masked
# cross-occurrence dependencies and malformed detached projections. These finite
# perturbations do not quantify over every possible response combination.
# FuzzTransitionOccurrenceJoint has four seeds and the same 18-shape grammar;
# it varies bounded raw register/memory, vector and outcome inputs independently.
# JointSameSiteApplication applies the same completed theorem twice at the same
# CALL address for four input valuations, checking fresh outcomes, current and
# residual bytes, exact invocation/anchor identities and actual parent RET, with
# wrong-anchor, numeric-first-hit and old-prefix-redirection refusal controls.
# The focused TestTransitionOccurrence* examples add sparse-ID/edge/frontier,
# join, ownership, resource, anchored-endpoint and call/return controls. Their
# finite fixtures and the oracle populations do not close the temporary gaps or
# establish source-loop correspondence, whole-source coverage or public authority.
# ConditionalOperation claims cover the separately checked outward distribution
# of Add/Sub/Equal/ULT/ULE/SLT/SLE through either bit-vector ITE operand under
# scalar-bitrelation RuleModel @4. The proposer supplies candidates, not premises.
# TestConditionalOperationEverySmallValuation exhausts widths 1..3, three word
# operands, both Boolean values, seven operators and two positions: 16,352
# valuations. WideBoundaries checks 32/64-bit eight-extrema products plus 128
# reproducible triples per operator/position/width, each with both Boolean values:
# 35,840 finite valuations, not exhaustive wide-state coverage.
# The other six ConditionalOperation tests cover a joined-counter frontier,
# malformed scoped inference and extra premises, cancellation/ownership/budgets,
# generated depth and shared node bounds, and Boolean-encoding normalization.
# Existing FuzzExactScalarSemantics claims include the extended two-position,
# independent-third-operand grammar and both condition-value seed families
# (230 seeds overall); existing LocalRuleAdversarialCrossProduct claims include
# the appended rule. These existing rows remain bound without duplicate claims.
# ApplicationExcludedRootReturn checks reclassification and false-guard replay of
# an excluded RET under its actual child activation. ReturnFrontierMustBeFalse
# separately refuses a feasible return frontier. ActivationConflictPath checks
# refusal at the conflicting callee with the exact derived entry path. These
# deciding controls supply no authorization to close the open native gaps.
# Narrow reference unit and generated-body claims exercise the production ABI,
# interpreter and specialization with synthetic typed bodies, not selected-action
# acquisition. NarrowGeneratedBodies checks 2,880 CAS32 input triples and 524,288
# byte logical evaluations across 64 register shapes per operation; these are
# finite populations, not exhaustive body or native-state coverage. The accumulator
# fuzzer retains independent full RAX, current32 and replacement32 inputs.
# TestTransferKernelLogicalValuesAndFlags exhausts all 65,536 byte operand pairs
# per AND/OR operation; its 32/64-bit cases are boundary and generated samples.
# The existing FuzzTransitionAtomicValues and FuzzAssemblyReferenceBodyAndPrivateFrame
# rows include their expanded narrow grammars without duplicate binding claims.
# TestNarrowReferenceSelectedRuntime acquires the actual current selected actions
# and checks the source from entry through narrow atomics, conditional live-object
# float bit views, the actual testAtomic64 invocation and finite round2 call to the
# actual return. It retains call-time heap and SSA value-map snapshots; this is
# conditional source transport, not native correspondence or rooted applicability.
# TestRegionNarrowSelectedReferenceApplications additionally checks same-block
# later writes against retained complete incoming, call-time and endpoint heaps.
# NarrowJoint generated/fuzz claims compare production conditional correspondence
# over actual selected fixture assembly and synthetic native regions, including
# complete returns, ordered effects, arbitrary initial globals and residual bytes.
# TestNarrowJointPrimitiveMetadataProbes only qualifies detached oracle assertions;
# it has no production-correspondence binding. TestGlobalFunctionAtomicNativeWidths
# checks the production classifier; TestNarrowJointCompleteAtomicWidthBoundary
# separately checks both matching-width full positives and cross-width refusals
# despite equal complete final bytes and registers. Operand-boundary claims stop
# before their actual instructions and supply no executed atomic or store effect.
# NarrowAccumulatorProvenance checks full-RAX scalar behavior and conservative
# CAS32 pointer metadata; it does not claim new positive pointer inference.

